# Tailscale's indicator in the connection area, the owner's plan of 2026-10-14 (phase 1, "make it
# visible on every port"; crates/mp-gui/src/tailscale.rs): after the link's state it reads this
# computer's Tailscale - here tests/gui/fake-tailscale.sh, which tools/gui-test.sh gives every
# script, on a tailnet as buzz-laptop - in Tailscale's own `status --json` words, its dot the OK
# colour. On a tailnet there is no first-start offer.
#
# Needs no link: tools/gui-headless.sh tailscale-indicator
screen fly
window 1600x1200
budget 8
env XDG_DATA_HOME $WORK
env MP_CONFIG_XML $WORK/config.xml
env FAKE_TAILSCALE_STATE running

within 12
expect tailscale.state on-tailnet
expect tailscale.shown true
expect tailscale.text Tailscale: on tailnet as buzz-laptop, 100.101.102.103
expect tailscale.name buzz-laptop
expect tailscale.address 100.101.102.103
expect tailscale.offer none
expect tailscale-indicator above status-row
expect tailscale-indicator below tab-fly
